.TH OPENCLOUDCMD 1 "2026-11-15" "OpenCloud Desktop 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opencloudcmd \- OpenCloud command line synchronization client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opencloudcmd
.RI [ options ]
.I server_url
.RI [ space_id ]
.RI [ source_dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opencloudcmd
performs the synchronization of an OpenCloud space to a local directory
without a graphical interface, suitable for scripts and headless setups.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I server_url
The URL of the OpenCloud installation, usually the root path.
.TP
.I space_id
The id, name or short id of the space to synchronize. If omitted or not
matching any space, a list of spaces is printed.
.TP
.I source_dir
The local directory to synchronize into.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " file"
Path to an exclude list file.
.TP
.BI \-\-unsynced-folders " file"
File containing the list of unsynced remote folders (selective sync).
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Do not block execution with interaction.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-sync-retries " n"
Retry the sync at most
.I n
times (defaults to 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-upload-limit " n"
Limit the upload speed to
.I n
KB/s.
.TP
.BI \-\-download-limit " n"
Limit the download speed to
.I n
KB/s.
.TP
.B \-\-sync-hidden-files
Enable synchronization of hidden files.
.TP
.BI \-\-verbose " verbosity"
Set the log verbosity: 0 = no logging (default), 1 = general logging,
2 = additionally HTTP logs, 3 = additionally debug information.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opencloud (1)
.SH AUTHOR
OpenCloud contributors.
